HST Office: a selected picture keeps its Picture Format tab on a short ribbon tab row.

1.0.3 made Writer's tab row longer (the Recently used tab and the AutoSave toggle at its start). Where the row is
too short for all tabs, ImplPlaceTabs left off every tab past the room before the menu button, that is the run
at the right end, and the contextual tab (Picture Format, Table Design, Shape Format...) always comes last: below
about 1050 px at 100 % on Linux, and in a window of a MacBook's width, a selected picture showed its handles but
no Picture Format tab, so its commands looked gone (they were only in the menu button's menu). 1.0.2 still
showed the tab at 960 px.

A short row now leaves off the tabs shown in every context first, from the right end (Extensions, Help, View...),
then the contextual tabs, then the File button, and the tabs kept close up from the row start. Without a
contextual tab nothing changes: the tabs left off are the run at the right end, as before. A tab left off stays
reachable from the menu button's menu and the KeyTips (HstIsOffRow). The decision is a plain function in
vcl/inc/HstRibbonTabsFit.hxx.

